This 9-line tail is identical at `:1348-1356`, differing only in the `skip_backdoor` argument (`false` there, `true` here):

```c
if(instance->mode == Iso15693PollerModeClone) {
    iso15693_poller_write_identity(instance, iso_poller);
    if(!iso15693_poller_write_source_blocks(instance, iso_poller, <bool>)) {
        iso15693_poller_report(instance, Iso15693PollerEventCardLost);
        return NfcCommandStop;
    }
}
iso15693_poller_report(instance, iso15693_poller_success_or_partial(instance));
return NfcCommandStop;
```

The 4-line CardLost preamble above each (`:1336-1339`, `:1415-1418`) is identical too.

Highest-value of the dedup items because of where it sits: this is the seam where a change to the gen2 verify silently fails to reach the gen1 verify. A `static NfcCommand iso15693_poller_finish_write(instance, iso_poller, bool skip_backdoor)` folds both.
